b6a6fed57beb94" "basis" 1160 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{3{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5ffccc056d43c528012bcb9c43d0684d0799657c1a2679280b6a6fed57beb94" "basis" 1160 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5ffccc056d43c528012bcb9c43d0684d0799657c1a2679280b6a6fed57beb94" "basis" 1160 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ed8cdcc837f8f61f51d4be69c4a88890296f8902d2343d7833a74b37d814ec2" "basis" 1198 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6{x}^{2})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(12x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-12\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-12\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-12(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-12D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{2}-12)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ed8cdcc837f8f61f51d4be69c4a88890296f8902d2343d7833a74b37d814ec2" "basis" 1198 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80c343f6220b0841b31908b283c2be395b14bd2eec8b7615fa78b6728d13d4ac" "basis" 1198 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ed8cdcc837f8f61f51d4be69c4a88890296f8902d2343d7833a74b37d814ec2" "basis" 1198 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-12708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡(x))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2x{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e53f22cf43eb485004dbcc35302eade2b8d3324c955d78a383237d5ac203d7e"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x(3{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] ["math" "2x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] ["math" "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] ["math" "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] ["math" "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{3{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-12708" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-49931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-49931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-49931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e53f22cf43eb485004dbcc35302eade2b8d3324c955d78a383237d5ac203d7e"} {"question" "q-49931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-49931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-49931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-114946" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-114946" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=25{x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}(5{x}^{5})-\\int (5{x}^{5})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10(\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D) \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{5}-10D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})+C\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-10D.$ Finally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & ={[{x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{5})]-[{1}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{5})] \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5-2+\\frac{2}{5})]-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-114946" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e53f22cf43eb485004dbcc35302eade2b8d3324c955d78a383237d5ac203d7e"} {"question" "q-114946" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-114946" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12{e}^{5}+2"] ["math" "\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{4{e}^{5}+3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{5}-2}{5}"] ["math" "{e}^{5}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-114946" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-352028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-352028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=27{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=54x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(27{x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(54x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+18\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 1\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+18\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+18(\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+D) \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=18D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =9{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2}-2-2 \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}-4 \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-352028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e53f22cf43eb485004dbcc35302eade2b8d3324c955d78a383237d5ac203d7e"} {"question" "q-352028" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-352028" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi^2-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6{x}^{2})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(12x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-12\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-12\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-12(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-12D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{2}-12)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e53f22cf43eb485004dbcc35302eade2b8d3324c955d78a383237d5ac203d7e"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi^2}{2}-12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/state.json" "file_sha256" "79c172c14c302f26027058c45d3e385afbab60719d5a0c934bcd4a71fa950910"} {"question" "q-49931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060738/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "9a6e69fb2f16f132684e7ce4129583ef8179ea087181ebea2509902d235720de" "reviewer_session" "01a118ea-3923-70c2-acd9-0830602bde5f" "rationale" "Integration by parts with u=2x² and dv=sin(2x)dx gives du=4x dx and v=−cos(2x)/2. Therefore the integral equals −x²cos(2x)+2∫x cos(2x)dx. Original option b (index 1) and the aut